*Case n ≡ 0 (mod 4):* n-2 = 2(odd), n+2 = 2(odd), so v₂(P) = 2. **Fails.**

*Case n ≡ 2 (mod 4):* n = 2k, k odd. Only (n-2),(n+2) contribute powers of 2. Setting j = (k-1)/2: v₂(P) = 4 + v₂(j) + v₂(j+1). Need ≥ 6, giving j ≡ 0 or 3 (mod 4), i.e., **n ≡ 2 or 14 (mod 16)**.

